For determining the number M of HARQ-ACK information bits for each DCI format 1_3 corresponding to the second HARQ-ACK sub-codebook in a PUCCH transmission:
M is a maximum number over all the configured cell set(s) S in a PUCCH group of the sum of NTB,cDL⋅NPDSCH,cmax (if nrofHARQ-BundlingGroups is not provided for a serving cell c) or NTB,cDL⋅NHARQ-ACK,cTBG,max (if nrofHARQ-BundlingGroups is provided for the serving cell c) across serving cells of a respective cell set S that can be co-scheduled by a DCI format 1_3;
NPDSCH,cmax is the maximum number of SLIVs amongst all rows of the multi-PDSCH TDRA table configured on the active BWP of the serving cell c;
NHARQ-ACK,cTBG,max is the maximum number of transport block groups (TBGs) for first TBs (and for second TBs, if configured) for the serving cell c if harq-ACKSpatialBundlingPUCCH is not provided, or the maximum number of PDSCH reception groups on the serving cell c if harq-ACKSpatialBundlingPUCCH is provided, and is provided by RRC parameter nrofHARQ-BundlingGroups;
NTB,cDL is the value of maxNrofCodeWordsScheduledByDCI for serving cell c when harq-ACKSpatialBundlingPUCCH is not provided; otherwise NTB,cDL=1.

